# Intent: Rollback on first-boot failure for a wirelessly installed image (release-and-updates.md: after install the unit must reach the host within 60 seconds or roll back, a hang included). The old rule confirmed any pending image after 20 seconds whatever the link did. Now the image is confirmed only after 20 seconds of uptime with the host link up; a timer armed at boot (outside the main loop, so a hang cannot stop it) marks the image invalid and reboots into the previous slot at 60 seconds. A confirmed image sends the firmware_update_validated event. Images flashed over USB are never pending, so they are unchanged.
# Placement: unit (the robot decides about its own boot slot)
# Upstream: main/hal/hal.cpp of the StackChan tree (MIT)
# Check after a flash: after a wireless update the log says "pending" at boot, then "reached the host; keeping it" within about 25 seconds; with the host stopped before the restart it says "Going back to the previous firmware" at 60 seconds and the unit boots the old version.
